Z||000000||overlord||02-08-2000||09:46 AM||||hi, i was reading about speakers down in one of the other posts, but no one said how to remove the headrest speakers.<P>first off , can this be done?<P>and second , howw  hard is it do put speakers in the side of the car (not in the headrests) i have a 84 2m4, so the rear speakrser are only in the headrest.<P>thnx.||||reg||3
Z||000001||lennyb4||02-08-2000||10:35 AM||||Mounting speakers in the rear body is not that difficult. I have a 87 coupe where the rear speakers are mounted on the side just above the seat. This might take a little cutting on the trim facia but you can cover that up with speaker grilles.The perfect tool to use would be either a dremil or a roto-zip (just bought one $60 and its a great tool) Or im not sure but maybe the interior trim from a later model would fit?||||reg||12
Z||000002||overlord||02-08-2000||11:03 AM||||ok..ive decided not to cut any holes in my baby..-)<P>and i just looked at the seats..HOW THE HECK DO U GET THE SPEAKERS OUT?<P>and if it involves cutting holes in the seat forget it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-08-2000||11:43 AM||||You need to remove the seat skin to replace the speakers. The seat is held on with "hogrings" You can get these at any upolstery shop and then carefully remove them and put them back on. Takes about an hour each seat.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SloPonti||02-08-2000||01:35 PM||||does anyone know what the  size of the speakers in the headrest are! i will replace them if they make a speaker for them!<BR>thanks]<BR>rob||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-08-2000||03:31 PM||||3.5"  Go to Crutchfield ( <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com" TARGET=_blank>www.crutchfield.com</A>  ).  They have 5 or 6 pairs of them ranging from about $60/pr to $100/pr.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ggarsk||02-08-2000||08:06 PM||||I unplugged the seat speakers in my '84. I have noticed that they get hot. And if you look at seats in the junk yard,you'll notice that some seats have been burned in the speaker area. The drivers seat in my patrs car is that way. I just put 2 6x9 Sony XPLODS in boxes behind my seat. With 2 4x6 Infinity's in the front and a 160 watt Pioneer CD player,I get all the sound I need.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||02-08-2000||10:17 PM||||Try a boneyard or better yet, here on the forum for sail panels from an '86 or later.  All of them had the speakers mounted in the sail panels instead of the seats.  I plan to take the panels out of my '86 and put them in my '85 whenever I get it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||pherder||02-09-2000||08:28 PM||||FYI, the speakers in the seats are 3" from the factory.<P>They just sit in a foam pocket so upgrading to 3.5" would not be hard.<P>Paul||||reg||4
Z||000009||Monkeyman||02-09-2000||08:38 PM||||3.5" from the factory according to what I've read, but it doesn't matter.  I'm probably wrong.||||reg||1
